curl_cffi is a Python binding for curl-impersonate via cffi. It can impersonate
the TLS/JA3 and HTTP/2 fingerprints of real browsers (Chrome, Safari, Firefox,
...), letting it fetch sites protected by TLS-fingerprint anti-bot systems that
plain requests/httpx cannot.

This port links the prebuilt FreeBSD libcurl-impersonate (the patched libcurl +
BoringSSL) that upstream ships starting with the 2.0.0 alpha releases, so no
BoringSSL build is required.
